            <ArticleTitle>Early exposure to germs and the Hygiene Hypothesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1210-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/cr.2012.65</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A recent paper suggests that reduced exposure to germs results in the expansion of a cell type called natural killer T cells, which predisposes to colitis and asthma. Such a scenario could explain the Hygiene Hypothesis, which has been a puzzle for decades.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
